{"base_rate":0.21145374449339208,"brier":0.07390220264317181,"bss":0.5567846135940411,"bss_hi":0.6463173134642067,"bss_lo":0.4662938300527068,"chart":{"base":[336.2,46.1],"fp":[219.7,340.5],"lead":"62,270.7 272,246.5 482,198.8 692,121.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.56 — higher than 97% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +6pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 81% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 82% → rained 77%"},"rel":"64.4,460.5 159.1,379 577,134.4"},"country":"MA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.025932452276064645,"ess":322.7870292567412,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Fes</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Fes rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 681 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 11.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.56, ranked 7 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(3&ndash;31) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>390</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Fes</b> <span class=\"muted\">Morocco</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.56</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>3&ndash;31\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>681 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Fes &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Fes\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.33430769230769,378.26666666666665 84.904,330.61176470588236 149.265625,245.5 296.8025,98.88888888888886 399.45828571428575,18.0 399.45828571428575,49.19999999999999 296.8025,174.72222222222223 149.265625,325.125 84.904,373.43529411764706 59.33430769230769,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"305.03083700440527\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"305.03083700440527\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.33430769230769,377.3333333333333 84.904,326.32941176470587 149.265625,285.3125 296.8025,144.38888888888889 399.45828571428575,59.60000000000002\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 390 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.33430769230769\" cy=\"377.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 15% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"84.904\" cy=\"326.32941176470587\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 26%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"149.265625\" cy=\"285.3125\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 65% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"296.8025\" cy=\"144.38888888888889\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"399.45828571428575\" cy=\"59.60000000000002\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(21%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Fes the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.71) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.13).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'>0.132</td><td class='num'>0.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>146</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.424</td><td class='num'>6.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.458</td><td class='num'>3.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.705</td><td class='num'>2.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":34.03313,"lon":-5.00028,"n":681,"n_cities":213,"name":"Fes","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0037692307692307686,"n":390,"obs":0.01282051282051282,"sig":true},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.076,"n":85,"obs":0.15294117647058825,"sig":true},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.2578125,"n":64,"obs":0.265625,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.6745833333333334,"n":72,"obs":0.6527777777777778,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9645714285714287,"n":70,"obs":0.8857142857142857,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":11.6,"provisional":false,"rank":7,"rank_hi":31.024999999999977,"rank_lo":3.0,"reliability":0.0014810260213690548,"resolution":0.09062182807784584,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"fes","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Casablanca"}